  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 7,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "aside_text",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.076,
            0.583,
            0.108,
            0.734
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Do You Know?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.309,
            0.085,
            0.652,
            0.101
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Metal + Dilute acid → Salt + Hydrogen"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.101,
            0.838,
            0.118
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "But do all metals react in the same manner? Let us find out.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.347,
            0.131,
            0.516,
            0.155
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 3.11"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.301,
            0.167,
            0.874,
            0.226
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Collect all the metal samples except sodium and potassium again. If the samples are tarnished, rub them clean with sand paper. CAUTION: Do not take sodium and potassium as they react vigorously even with cold water.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.301,
            0.226,
            0.874,
            0.255
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Put the samples separately in test tubes containing dilute hydrochloric acid.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.301,
            0.255,
            0.875,
            0.283
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Suspend thermometers in the test tubes, so that their bulbs are dipped in the acid.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.301,
            0.283,
            0.752,
            0.299
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Observe the rate of formation of bubbles carefully.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.301,
            0.298,
            0.862,
            0.314
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Which metals reacted vigorously with dilute hydrochloric acid?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.302,
            0.313,
            0.827,
            0.328
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "With which metal did you record the highest temperature?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.301,
            0.328,
            0.874,
            0.357
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Arrange the metals in the decreasing order of reactivity with dilute acids.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.276,
            0.372,
            0.898,
            0.405
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Write equations for the reactions of magnesium, aluminium, zinc and iron with dilute hydrochloric acid.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.275,
            0.405,
            0.899,
            0.486
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hydrogen gas is not evolved when a metal reacts with nitric acid. It is",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " because "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{HNO_{3}}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is a strong oxidising agent. It oxidises the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { H } _ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "produced to water and itself gets reduced to any of the nitrogen oxides",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { ( N _ { 2 } O }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ",",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " NO, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { N O _ { 2 } ) }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". But magnesium (Mg) and manganese (Mn) react with very dilute",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{HNO_{_3}}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " to evolve "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { H } _ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "gas.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.275,
            0.485,
            0.9,
            0.582
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You must have observed in Activity 3.11, that the rate of formation of bubbles was the fastest in the case of magnesium. The reaction was also the most exothermic in this case. The reactivity decreases in the order",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{Mg}>\\mathrm{Al}>\\mathrm{Zn}>\\mathrm{Fe}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". In the case of copper, no bubbles were seen and the temperature also remained unchanged. This shows that copper does not react with dilute HCl.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.624,
            0.864,
            0.713
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Aqua regia, (Latin for ‘royal water’) is a freshly prepared mixture of concentrated hydrochloric acid and concentrated nitric acid in the ratio of 3:1. It can dissolve gold, even though neither of these acids can do so alone. Aqua regia is a highly corrosive, fuming liquid. It is one of the few reagents that is able to dissolve gold and platinum.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.278,
            0.732,
            0.899,
            0.773
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3.2.4 How do Metals react with Solutions of other Metal Salts?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.347,
            0.785,
            0.519,
            0.808
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 3.12"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.301,
            0.818,
            0.708,
            0.833
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Take a clean wire of copper and an iron nail.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.092,
            0.917,
            0.12,
            0.931
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "44"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.301,
            0.833,
            0.874,
            0.862
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Put the copper wire in a solution of iron sulphate and the iron nail in a solution of copper sulphate taken in test tubes (Fig. 3.4).",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.301,
            0.862,
            0.696,
            0.878
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Record your observations after 20 minutes.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.831,
            0.916,
            0.899,
            0.929
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Science"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 22,
